        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "606ecd0b-ae63-5a03-9729-24e5d0b4aabb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Breeds: Stabyhoun, Griffon Bruxellois, Griffon Belge, Petit Brabançon, Glen of Imaal Terrier, Cavalier King Charles Spaniel\n- Concepts: Rare dog breeds, Canine Chiari-like malformation\n\nFacts:\n- The Stabyhoun, also called the Stabij, is one of the five rarest dog breeds in the world.\n- Rare breed (dog) refers to any dog breed that exists in small numbers.\n- Rare breed (dog) can refer to old established breeds such as the Stabyhoun and the Glen of Imaal Terrier, as well as newer creations.\n- The term Griffon Bruxellois may refer to three different breeds: the Griffon Bruxellois, the Griffon Belge, and the Petit Brabançon.\n- Canine Chiari-like malformation is rare in most dog breeds.\n- Canine Chiari-like malformation has reportedly become very widespread in the Cavalier King Charles Spaniel and the Griffon Bruxellois, also called the Brussels Griffon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
